    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/clinical-instructional-preceptor-physician-assistant-studies-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Job Description for the Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position.",
      "description": "Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Academic Affairs Temporary Add to favorites View favorites Title: Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies Position Type: Temporary Days Per Week: Varies Hours Per Week: VP Area: Office of the Provost and Academic Affairs Department: School of Health Sciences Position Summary Seeking qualified providers (MD, DO, PA, or NP) with an interest and passion for assisting pre-licensure PA students in developing clinical competence and critical thinking skills in a variety of clinical learning environments. Clinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in a variety of clinical settings. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Preceptor Benefits: • Payment is competitive and dependent upon the payment model of the preceptor's institution. • Cat 1 CME from AAPA for PA preceptors • Pipeline to future colleagues: Build connections and interview potential candidates for your job openings Minimum Required Education and Experience A relevant training degree is required. Must hold an active state license as MD, DO, PA, or relevant NP training and have at least one year of clinical experience. Physicians must also be board certified in their area of practice. NP example—a psychiatric mental health NP can provide a behavioral medicine experience, or a board-certified pediatrician can provide a pediatric experience. Required Other Training, Certifications, or Licensing Must hold an active state license and appropriate board certification as above Permission of the clinical site to host students (affiliation agreement required) Job Duties Clinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in one of the following medical settings: -Pediatrics: 6-week experiences -Inpatient Medicine (hospitalist): 6-week experiences -Women’s Health: 3-week experiences The preceptor assesses student performance during clinical experiences using provided evaluation tools and provides constructive feedback for growth: -Demonstrates effective clinical skills according to evidence-based practices. -Serves as a professional role model for students and fosters a positive and -professional learning environment that respects diversity, equity, and inclusion. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert c86458c0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at 