    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/adjunct-instructor-sport-management-department-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Academic Affairs Adjunct Add to favorites View favorites Part-time instructors in Sport Management – Elon University JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Department of Sport Management at Elon University seeks to hire part-time instructors for in-person classes (on Elon's main campus) for the spring 2026 semester, as well as the 2026-2027 academic year. These appointments are part-time, non-tenure track, with no guarantee of renewal. Our classes will be in-person either M-W-F, for 70 minutes each class, or T-TH, for 100 minutes each class. We also have a few M-W afternoon classes, for 100 minutes each class. Courses include, but are not limited to: Sport Law, Sport & Media, Sport Communications, Research Methods, Event & Venue Management, Sport Marketing, Sport Promotion & Sales, and Sport Finance. A terminal degree in sport management or other closely related field is preferred. Candidates should have teaching experience, as well as professional experience in sport management industries/fields. Applicants must demonstrate a commitment to inclusive, student-centered teaching and clear, skills-based assessment.Applicants should apply by submitting a short letter of interest with their qualifications, current Curriculum Vita (CV) and contact information of at least three references. Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and positions filled as needed. For information about Elon University’s Sport Management Department, please visit https://www.elon.edu/u/academics/communications/sport-management/ Elon University is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff and student body and welcomes all applicants. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert ebd23fb7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Communications School of Communications Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 2c762ff7 Last Name (required) 82f3f5c8 Email (required) a7e9a417 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Director of Health and Well-Being Initiatives Using knowledge of and experience with: innovative health and wellness initiatives for staff, faculty, undergraduate and graduate students, teaching, research, and leadership in a postsecondary institution as well as with: theory and academic scholarship to design, implement, and evaluate effective programs, services, and interventions; eliciting university-wide buying, readiness for collaboration and consultation with colleagues; executing strategic initiatives; building partnerships; relating effectively with a diverse range of university constituents and stakeholders; generating sole and collaborative academic scholarship for publications and national and international presentations; mentoring student research; working with diverse populations; and strategic planning and assessment: provide sustained and visible campus leadership for holistic health and wellbeing; engage and collaborate with campus faculty and staff to link curricular and co-curricular experiences to the goals of the HealthEU initiative; coordinate with leaders of initiatives in each of the six dimensions of wellbeing described in HealthEU to track and share progress and to develop innovative collaborations that support research and understanding of best practices in advancing well-being; regularly assess and communicate the impact and effectiveness of HealthEU initiatives; coordinate opportunities for faculty scholarship, creative work, and teaching to connect with HealthEU goals; co-chair the university-wide HealthEU Council; assist with planning and development of an engaging, vibrant new campus facility for integrated health and wellness; coordinate activities and operations related to research on collegiate health and wellbeing. co-supervise the Faculty Fellow for Wellness; establish collaborative goals for HealthEU initiatives and provide direct oversight for budgets, priorities, and plans for collaborative strategies that advance those goals; serve as a clearinghouse for resources, education, and collaborative programming related to health and wellbeing Participate in university events, celebrations, and traditions; serve on university, divisional, or departmental committees, task forces, and search committees; other duties as assigned by the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs. \"This employer is an institution of higher education under 20 CFR 656.40(e). Assistant Professor of Religious Studies Use knowledge of and work experience with teaching Theology/Religious Studies-related undergraduate and graduate courses to teach grad and undergraduate courses in religion and religious ethics, and Elon’s Core Curriculum. Work with Religious Studies faculty to continuously improve the curriculum of the Religious Studies major. Conduct academic research in Religious Studies. Mentor students in their degree progress, course plan, and academic research. Participate in the services and activities at department and university levels to support the life and progress of the university including undergraduate research, studying abroad, serving on university and school committees, and advising student organizations. Create a constant stream of scholarly publications and contribute to the life of the university through service. Part time custodian weekends Sat & Sun 9am-12pm Facilities Management The custodian position is responsible for helping maintain a clean and safe environment of all inside spaces which include Residential housing, Academic buildings, Athletic facilities, Student centers and dining locations for Elon University Campus. This includes, but not limited to, maintain and cleaning equipment, the cleaning and sanitizing of bathrooms, vacuuming floors, and removing all trash from the premises, cleaning of biohazards and high touch areas. Custodians are also responsible for monitoring special events and athletic games across campus making sure areas are clean and sanitized during events. Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Program Assistant, School of Communications School of Communications Program Assistant, School of Communications\n\nThe program assistant position in the School of Communications reports to the director of student engagement and special projects & instructor of journalism. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon School of Health Sciences Elon University, renowned as a model for engaged learning, in partnership with the national search firm, Scott Healy & Associates, invites applications and nominations for five Principal Faculty positions for its Physician Assistant Program located in Elon, NC due to the program expanding its cohort size, with the new class that matriculated in January 2026.  These faculty members will help to develop and implement curricular aspects of a fully accredited program in Physician Assistant (PA) Studies.\n\nThe anticipated start date for the position is Summer 2026. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) e478e2d7 Last Name (required) 7cc7dcb4 Email (required) 3cdedd74 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Non-Discrimination Statement Elon University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin (including shared ancestry or ethnic characteristics), sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity, and pregnancy or related conditions), age, disability, genetic information, religion, veteran’s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law (collectively, “Protected Categories”) in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Quick Links Title IX Privacy Policy Emergency Information Our Culture and Diversity Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Elon University . Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Elon Social Media Page Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/project-manager-integration-queens-campus-charlotte-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Job Description for the Project Manager, Integration position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position.",
      "description": "Project Manager, Integration - Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States About Benefits Human Resources Working at Elon View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Job Description for the Project Manager, Integration position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Project Manager, Integration Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, 28216 University Administration University Operations Staff Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Project Manager, Integration Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Monday - Friday Hours Per Week: 40 hrs/wk VP Area: Office of the President Department: President's Office Location: Queens Campus - Charlotte Position Summary The Project Manager supports the Chief Integration Officer and Deputy CIO by coordinating projects that advance integration, shared services, youth engagement, stakeholder engagement, community outreach, student recruitment, and office management. This position plays an important supporting role for the Integration Team, helping track project timelines, deliverables, and expenses; communicating with, coordinating projects, and setting meetings with sub-team members; and providing research and coordination support across a range of integration initiatives. The project manager assists the CIO and Deputy CIO to research and build out key initiatives such as youth engagement programs, access and success programs, Queens and Elon campus employee visit programs, communications across Elon and Queens campuses, and more. Part of the project manager’s role will include calendaring, budget tracking, and minor travel arrangements for the CIO. At times the Project Manager may also provide assistance to the enrollment team with recruitment of transfer students. This position is in-person and based in Charlotte, North Carolina. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience Bachelor's degree with a minimum of 1–3 years — Experience in higher education administration, project management, admissions, alumni relations, or community engagement. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple tasks and projects with accuracy and follow-through. Experience working with diverse stakeholders and building community relationships preferred. Preferred Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in higher education, communications, business, public relations, or a related field; Master’s degree a plus. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong organizational and project management skills, with attention to detail and the ability to meet deadlines. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and Google Workspace. Familiarity with CRM platforms or enrollment management systems a plus. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively across teams and with external partners. Curiosity, initiative, and a relationship-oriented approach to work. Knowledge of Charlotte’s civic, nonprofit, and business community preferred. Familiarity with Elon or Queens programs and culture a plus. Job Duties Support the CIO and Deputy CIO on assigned projects and integration team priorities, including tracking action items and deadlines, preparing project documentation, coordinating inter-departmental communication, and ensuring timely follow-through on deliverables. Assist the CIO and Deputy CIO with projects and documents related to the development of integration initiatives, tracking of milestones, inter-team communication, material and agenda preparation, and accountability for key deliverables. Assist the CIO and Deputy with event planning, stakeholder outreach/engagement, employee engagement across campuses, professional development sessions, etc. Assist the Deputy CIO with Elon and Queens integration-related events at the institutional, alumni, and community level, including listening tours, stakeholder forums, joint campus visits, alumni gatherings, professional development offerings, and signature integration events. Support event strategy, logistics, and follow-up in collaboration with communications and advancement teams. Support relationships with alumni from both Elon and Queens, including identifying opportunities for alumni engagement in integration initiatives, supporting alumni listening sessions and events, and contributing to cultivation strategies in partnership with advancement and alumni affairs teams. Support and assist the CIO by managing calendaring, meeting coordination, limited travel arrangements, budget processes/tracking, and presentation preparation as needed. Conduct research and provide analytical support on topics relevant to the integration, including peer institution benchmarking, market and demographic data, program development opportunities, community partnership models, civic organizations, business partners, nonprofit entities, and community events, and partnerships in the Charlotte region. Research relevant to the integration’s engagement and visibility goals. Synthesize research findings into clear, actionable summaries for leadership. Support Admissions and enrollment-related projects for both the Elon Charlotte and Queens campuses, including assisting with recruitment events, management of prospective student communications, and logistical support for admissions initiatives. Collaborate with Admissions teams. Special Instructions to Applicants: Some evening and weekend work may be required. Travel required. Regular travel between Elon’s Burlington/Alamance County campus (monthly), the Queens University campus in Charlotte, and the Elon Charlotte offices. Occasional travel for professional meetings and events. This position offers an exceptional opportunity to contribute to a landmark moment in the history of two universities. The Project Manager will be embedded in the day-to-day work of a high-energy integration office and will develop deep knowledge of both institutions and the Charlotte community. The successful candidate will be highly organized, a self-starter, and genuinely excited about connecting people and institutions in service of student success and community impact. Regular work in both Charlotte and occasional travel to Elon’s main campus are expected. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert a09cd661 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments President's Office President's Office Locations Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 5ef629ab Last Name (required) 71689dfd Email (required) 009f7fe7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Director of Health and Well-Being Initiatives Using knowledge of and experience with: innovative health and wellness initiatives for staff, faculty, undergraduate and graduate students, teaching, research, and leadership in a postsecondary institution as well as with: theory and academic scholarship to design, implement, and evaluate effective programs, services, and interventions; eliciting university-wide buying, readiness for collaboration and consultation with colleagues; executing strategic initiatives; building partnerships; relating effectively with a diverse range of university constituents and stakeholders; generating sole and collaborative academic scholarship for publications and national and international presentations; mentoring student research; working with diverse populations; and strategic planning and assessment: provide sustained and visible campus leadership for holistic health and wellbeing; engage and collaborate with campus faculty and staff to link curricular and co-curricular experiences to the goals of the HealthEU initiative; coordinate with leaders of initiatives in each of the six dimensions of wellbeing described in HealthEU to track and share progress and to develop innovative collaborations that support research and understanding of best practices in advancing well-being; regularly assess and communic